+Before encoding, the P25 voice path applies a fixed 12 dB (4x) PCM calibration, then the microphone gain, with
+saturation. The previous level was about 14 dB below the pinned Yazev IMBE reference encoder on the same harmonic
+signal. With the calibration, the transmitted frames decoded through both that reference and mbelib measured within
+2.2 dB of the reference encoder's level. This is a transmit-input calibration only: the decoder and its golden vectors
+are unchanged. YSF VW uses the same voice path and calibration. The microphone setting remains 2 dB per step around
+step 5.
+
